From 468a2cc4945780b3b865500cf2d65da3b172a8c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 17:32:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03316/11362] [outer-loop] arc: wire prior_state into the live
 agent behind the trust gate

Completes the capture->prior pipeline into the live solver. E3AgentPolicy._induce_and_plan now tries a
per-game world model LEARNED from the played transitions FIRST -- warm-started from the cross-game CNN
prior (models/arc_dynamics_prior.pt, transfers 5/5) -- GATED by the same >=0.5 held-out trust bar the LLM
path uses. If it earns trust and plans a win it is used (zero-LLM, execution-grounded); otherwise it falls
through to the existing LLM induction. Non-fatal try/except -- can never break the existing path.

- arc_live_ttt.gated_engine_from_transitions(): loads the prior, warm-starts a LiveTTTWorldModel, fits on
  a train split, and returns (engine, is_level_complete) ONLY if held-out exact-grid accuracy >=
  trust_threshold (else None -> fallback preserved). Standalone, fully tested offline.
- LiveTTTWorldModel: cnn_epochs=40 (LIGHT live fine-tuning -- 400 was too slow for per-induction use AND
  tripped the test memory guard; warm-starting from the prior means few epochs suffice).
- arc_competition_agent._induce_and_plan: the minimal gated TTT-first attempt (one localized block before
  the LLM paths).

Validated: 3 gate tests + 5 live-ttt tests green; make_carnot_agent imports/builds; SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG
parity test 10/10 (the 0.08-incident guard intact). The gate currently engages on games where the learned
model reaches >=0.5 exact-match (e.g. the gravity-class) and falls back otherwise; it engages more as the
representation improves (object-delta + TRM are the next levers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
